	"notes": "The federal government's own design system homepage is built the same way as several marketing sites in this batch: full-width painted bands (a banner, the header, the hero, a row of features, a showcase of real government sites, the footer), each holding its content in a 1400px column that centres itself once the window is wide enough. The one thing that sets it apart from the rest of this batch is how its breakpoints are written: every single one is in em or rem units, never plain pixels, which is why the automatic px-breakpoint scan found none at all even though the page clearly does respond. An em-based breakpoint is an accessibility choice — it moves together with a reader's own font-size setting rather than staying fixed at a pixel number, which fits a site whose whole purpose is teaching government agencies to build accessible websites.",
